    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Initial Deal**: 5 cards each. Initial betting round. 2. **Repeated Draw Phases**: Each active player must choose one of three options: \n   - **All for One**: Discard your entire 5-card hand and draw 5 new ones.\n   - **One for All**: Discard exactly 1 card and draw 1 new one.\n   - **Stand Pat**: Keep your current hand (once you stand pat, you cannot draw in future rounds).\n3. **Betting**: Each draw phase is followed by a full betting round. 4. **Repetition**: Draw and betting rounds continue until the deck has too few cards left to fulfill a worst-case draw scenario (i.e., every participant drawing 5). 5. **Showdown**: Remaining players reveal hands. Best hand according to standard rankings wins.',
    Player: '1. **Initial Deal**: 5 cards each. Initial betting round. 2. **Repeated Draw Phases**: Each active player must choose one of three options: \n   - **All for One**: Discard your entire 5-card hand and draw 5 new ones.\n   - **One for All**: Discard exactly 1 card and draw 1 new one.\n   - **Stand Pat**: Keep your current hand (once you stand pat, you cannot draw in future rounds).\n3. **Betting**: Each draw phase is followed by a full betting round. 4. **Repetition**: Draw and betting rounds continue until the deck has too few cards left to fulfill a worst-case draw scenario (i.e., every participant drawing 5). 5. **Showdown**: Remaining players reveal hands. Best hand according to standard rankings wins.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the best 5-card poker hand at showdown or by forcing all other players to fold.',
    gameplay: '1. **Initial Deal**: 5 cards each. Initial betting round. 2. **Repeated Draw Phases**: Each active player must choose one of three options: \n   - **All for One**: Discard your entire 5-card hand and draw 5 new ones.\n   - **One for All**: Discard exactly 1 card and draw 1 new one.\n   - **Stand Pat**: Keep your current hand (once you stand pat, you cannot draw in future rounds).\n3. **Betting**: Each draw phase is followed by a full betting round. 4. **Repetition**: Draw and betting rounds continue until the deck has too few cards left to fulfill a worst-case draw scenario (i.e., every participant drawing 5). 5. **Showdown**: Remaining players reveal hands. Best hand according to standard rankings wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'No half-measures: You cannot discard 2, 3, or 4 cards. It is strictly 1 or 5 or 0.',
      'Standing Pat: Once a player stands pat, they are locked into that hand for the remainder of the deal.',
      'End Condition: The game ends automatically when the deck contains fewer than (Active Players * 5) cards, or by mutual agreement if betting becomes circular.',
    ],
